+    `The server's playful policy overrides generic game/Skill defaults, including a user-template gameType=quiz or scoring=10/speedBonus=5.\n` +
+    `For a game page, the AI designs a puzzle, strategy or card task from the locked learning objective. Never make a quiz game. Show a concise goal and rules, manipulable teaching objects, state-computed consequences, explanatory feedback, recoverable mistakes and working restart/replay. Keep game.questions absent; widget-config scoring is {"correctPoints":0}, with no bonuses or achievements. Local feedback must never emit official score, mastery, reward or completion events.\n` +
+    `For a quantitative/grouping/fraction/ratio/percentage mathematics brief, the lesson includes real interactive 3D linked to the objective: actual geometry/projection with meaningful rotate, select and split/regroup operations. If this is its 3D/game page, implement that model rather than decorative rotation or CSS perspective. Stay within allowed content; do not introduce volume formulas or advanced solids. Preserve any independently required numeric SVG model as evidence. Other math and language choose 2D/3D for teaching need; language does not require 3D.\n` +
+    `Use short visible instructions and a large model. A short demonstration leads to learner operation, observable consequence and a brief reason. In actions, narrate the actual controls and feedback in short steps; do not dictate an independent answer or describe nonexistent interaction. In content, implement the controls and computed feedback, not a static promise of a game.\n` +
+    `Keep the four locked question IDs, text and options unchanged: the guided pair share one earlier quiz page, the independent pair share one later quiz page after exploration. If this is a quiz, generate only its assigned pair, hasAnswer=false and answer=[]. Never duplicate assessments in the game or add scored questions.\n` +
+    `Honor the page brief's model, misconception, feedback and transition, existing multistate probes/reset, exact grade/difficulty, source attribution and all original quality rules. Planning language stays private; output only this page/phase.`;
+}
+
+export const MIRA_FORMAL_PLAYFUL_REVIEW_VERSION = 'mira.formal-course-review.v5-playful-context' as const;
+export function formalPlayfulReviewInstructions(context: MiraFormalPlayfulContext): string {
+  assertContext(context);
+  return `\nADDITIONAL SERVER PLAYFUL REVIEW v1:\n` +
+    `Audit playfulLearning against actual persisted HTML/JS, narration, visible text and browser observations, not its self-description or game label. The AI must have designed a knowledge-dependent game with a child-readable goal and concise rules, meaningful model manipulation, state-computed result, explanatory feedback, a recoverable unsuccessful attempt and a working restart/replay. Reject disguised quizzes, click counters, canned answer reveals, extra assessment items or local rewards presented as official learning credit.\n` +
+    `For math briefs teaching quantities/grouping/fractions/ratios/percentages, require an actual manipulable 3D teaching model with real geometry/projection and meaningful rotate, select and split/regroup operations linked to the locked objective. A 2D game, tilted card, decorative 3D or camera-only orbit cannot satisfy that requirement. Reject unsupported claims of 3D, missing operations and advanced volume/solid concepts outside the grade boundary. Preserve the registered numeric SVG evidence; 3D never replaces its independent quantitative check. Language does not require 3D.\n` +
+    `Verify a short demonstration -> learner operation -> visible consequence -> brief explanation -> retry teaching rhythm, concise reading, the guided pair together after exploration and independent pair together later, with all four locked questions unchanged. Mark meaningful_interaction, teaching_sequence, grade_fit, language_load or assessment_alignment false as applicable when a playful requirement fails; cite actual scene evidence and a concrete repair. Never treat the metadata or this prompt as evidence of successful play.\n`;
 }
 
